 Film Grain Studio formal stable baseline
 
 Baseline:
-v4.5.2.2
+v4.6.0
 
 Supersedes:
-v4.5.2
+v4.5.2.2
 
 Major changes:
-- Fixes the Batch Summary timer compatibility issue that could make Started, Completed, and Elapsed all show Unavailable on some Windows / PowerShell environments.
-- Timer values are queried independently instead of returning multiple comma-separated values through one PowerShell command.
-- Elapsed time is calculated as integer seconds and formatted by BAT as cumulative HH:mm:ss.
-- Adds a DATE / TIME BAT fallback so Batch Summary timing remains available when the PowerShell timing query fails.
-- GUI and CLI continue to use the same timer implementation in the shared StudioBridge core.
-- No AV1 / HEVC / x264 encoding parameters or previously validated processing behavior were changed.
+- Adds AV1 NVENC multi-engine Split Frame Encoding (SFE) for Standard and UHQ.
+- Detects the usable NVENC engine count dynamically; no GPU model hardcoding.
+- Requires grav1synth 0.2.2+ before the SFE checkbox can be enabled.
+- Keeps AV1 FAST, HEVC, x264, and AV1 no-reencode SFE disabled by policy based on actual pipeline testing.
+- Fixes interlaced input with Interpolation enabled: progressive inputs continue through OpenSVPFlow 60 fps, while interlaced inputs automatically bypass OpenSVPFlow and use the existing field-rate deinterlace path.
+- Preserves GUI / CLI synchronization through the shared StudioBridge core.
+- Keeps v4.5.2.2 Batch Summary timing compatibility fixes and existing AAC 256k, Grain, LUT, subtitle, Cinematic, upload, and MPEG-TS sync behavior.
 
 Validation:
-The v4.5.2.2 timer compatibility fix was user-tested successfully on both the laptop and desktop systems before formal release.
+- RTX 4080: SFE engine count detected as x2.
+- AV1 Standard and AV1 UHQ SFE paths user-tested successfully with grav1synth 0.2.2-compatible build.
+- Interlaced .ts input with Interpolation enabled user-tested successfully using automatic field-rate deinterlace fallback.
 
-Preserved baseline behavior:
-All v4.5.2 AV1 / HEVC / x264 bitrate-policy behavior, Grain / LUT / subtitle / deinterlace / OpenSVPFlow paths, H.264 upload behavior, AAC 256k policy, standalone tool behavior, and Batch Summary timing scope remain intact.
+Formal release:
+FilmGrain_Studio_v4.6.0_Stable.zip
